# trainer.phext — the training-film production process

This phext packages a PROCESS, not a film: the way Will Bickford and
Emise developed, across three rounds in November 2026, for making a
training film about Phext Edit ("The Encyclopedia You Can Carry").
Another mind — a future Emise, a Choir seat, a new agent — should be
able to pick this up and run a training film the same way: same
discipline, same gates, same honesty about what was faked (nothing)
and what was substituted (declared, on the record).

Provenance: Will's direction, 2026-11-11 00:30 CST — "package up
this as trainer.phext — publish it into human.git" — clarified in
the same minute: "(this being the process we've developed)". Task
coordinate: 48.5.9/7.6.11/6.5.9. Built 2026-11-11 from the working
files in ~/workspace/phext-walkthrough/; published to
wbic16/human@exo. Coordinates in this file are internal to
trainer.phext.

## How to use it

Read the ten stage scrolls in order (Collection 2) before your
first round; they are the process. The worked example (Collection
3) is the evidence: the actual plan, scripts, briefs, and
production logs of the film this process produced, inscribed in
full. When a stage scroll and a worked-example scroll disagree,
the stage scroll is the distilled rule and the log is what
actually happened — both are kept on purpose.

## The process map

1. 1.1.1/2.1.1/1.1.1 — Brief & grounding: how a round starts
2. 1.1.1/2.1.2/1.1.1 — Claim verification: test before you write
3. 1.1.1/2.1.3/1.1.1 — Demo build: a real artifact, measured
4. 1.1.1/2.1.4/1.1.1 — Narration: voice, sections, timing
5. 1.1.1/2.1.5/1.1.1 — Capture & render: ranch-only, thermally gated
6. 1.1.1/2.1.6/1.1.1 — Style direction: notes into instructions
7. 1.1.1/2.1.7/1.1.1 — Assembly & audio finish
8. 1.1.1/2.1.8/1.1.1 — Verification & delivery
9. 1.1.1/2.1.9/1.1.1 — Revision rounds & correction propagation
10. 1.1.1/2.1.10/1.1.1 — Standing rules the process runs under

Worked example (Collection 3): the production plan, the original
walkthrough script and shot list, the three round scripts, the two
written revision briefs, the three production logs, the demo2
encyclopedia's README and link-verification record, and a
filmography of the cuts. The videos themselves are not embedded
(too large for the repo); the filmography scroll names each cut's
file, size, and SHA-256 so any copy can be verified.

A note on counts: three scripts exist (R1, R2, R3) and two written
revision briefs (R2, R3). Round 1 had no separate brief file — its
direction was Will's delivery of Emi Prime's revised script plus
the re-run order, and it is represented by its script and its
production log.

State at packaging (2026-11-11 ~00:40 CST): Rounds 1 and 2 are
complete and delivered. Round 3 is MID-FLIGHT — SCRIPT-R3.md is
complete (inscribed at 1.1.1/3.2.3/1.1.1) and its narration was
