## 5. Production notes

**Operative plan:** PRODUCTION-PLAN.md **§6 (Polish Tier)** governs
production — two-pass edit with gates, rendered motion-graphics
package, key-frame-standard Scrolltown foreshadow, finished audio,
~55 minutes of Will's time total (script approval ~15 + Gate 1
~25 + Gate 2 ~15; no one-time sample, no narration sitting).
Will does not narrate (his correction, 2026-11-09), and he ruled
the voice himself (2026-11-09 23:19 CST): **"You narrate it,
Emise"** — narration is Route C, Emise/Aria TTS, per
PRODUCTION-PLAN §6.3 (clone and VO-artist routes documented there
as evaluated alternatives not taken). Narration speed is
**100% for the video** (Will, 2026-11-09 23:26 CST; his 120%
voice-note preference is separate). The full narration track is
rendered: `narration/beat-01.mp3` … `beat-12.mp3` +
`narration-full.mp3` (1,005 words, 364.2 s measured; source
`narration-script.txt`, timing sheet `narration/TIMING.md`),
riding Gate 1 as the voice proof. The checklist
below remains the capture-day reference; where it and §6 differ
(edit estimates, finishing steps), §6 wins.

**Recording checklist (capture in this order)**

1. Terminal block first (it's deterministic): `query_demo.py toc`,
   `get 1.1.1/2.1.2/2.1.1` (Oak), `edit` demo on a scratch copy,
   byte-diff summary, `xz -9` seal size. Script + commands in `demo/`.
2. Plain-editor raw-file scroll (any editor; use demo/wiki.phext).
3. Browser block at edit.phext.io: fresh-tab load, browse, coordinate
   jump, search, one-line edit, save. Clear cookies first so the
   signed-out experience is what's on camera.
4. Cutaway stack-diagram slide (build once, reuse in the cutdown).
5. End card.

**Confirm during recording (not asserted as fact anywhere above)**

- Which phext the site offers a signed-out visitor (demo/welcome
  content, its name, and whether browsing it needs sign-in today).
- Exact on-screen labels/gestures for: opening a phext, the dimension
  navigation UI, coordinate jump, search box, save. (Capabilities are
  verified from the phext-lattice repo — Navigator/search/overlay-save
  are real — but the hosted UI's exact presentation is checked on the
  day, and B-roll follows the checker, not this script.)
- Whether the hosted editor offers a visitor a download/export of
  the phext being browsed. Source check (phext-lattice): the only
  download endpoint in the editor source is the submissions review
  queue — so plan on the fallback in the 5:15 beat (open demo/
  wiki.phext in the plain editor) unless the live site proves
  otherwise on the day.
- Whether a custom phext (e.g. demo/wiki.phext) can be loaded into the
  hosted editor by a visitor, and how (the repo documents /submit as
  a *signed-in* upload-for-review flow — do not present it as a
  no-login import). If wiki.phext can't be shown in the hosted editor,
  the script already carries the concept on the site's own content and
  the proof on the local file.
- The current public utilities list on the site (Up Goer Five,
  Coordinate TTS demo, Learn You Phext per the standing record).

**Runtime estimate (estimate, labelled):** narration measures 1,029 spoken
words (989 + the 40-word Scrolltown foreshadow draft) ≈ 7.4 min at 140 wpm, plus demo pauses (page loads, terminal
runs) that are performed, not spoken — inside the 6–8 min target,
near its top; trim the 1:20 explainer first if the read runs long. Recording + screen capture ≈ 45–75 min;
edit ≈ half a day. All estimates, not measurements.

**Claims to avoid**

- ❌ "Wikipedia has been converted to phext" / any implication the
  full Wikipedia is in the box. The claim is architectural: an
  encyclopedia *can* be carried this way; the demo is 24 articles.
- ❌ Any performance number not measured in the demo README or cited
  from the phext-lattice README / phcc repo (no "100× faster" claims).
- ❌ "No server at all" for the hosted editor — edit.phext.io is a
  hosted web app. The no-backend claim is about *your data's* shape:
  the file carries itself; SQ/edit are thin hosts, not a DBMS.
- ❌ A no-login *import/upload* flow (see confirm list).
- ❌ SQL comparisons beyond the framing ("no query language needed
  for this") — don't claim phext replaces databases generally.
- ❌ "A normal editor shows you the dimensions / it looks just as
  good raw." It doesn't — the raw view is text plus separator marks.
  The contrast is the claim; don't sand it down.
- ❌ Coordinates as global/unique across files — coordinates are
  internal to each phext; say "in this file" when it matters.
