- Beat **07 (edit + save) remains a GAP** for the signed-in
  session: anonymous routes cannot save by design, and nothing
  was faked. The editor's Search sheet also could not be held
  open under automation (two honestly-labelled attempt frames);
  beat 06 is covered by the Previewer pair regardless.
- The OBS route below still governs **motion takes** (Session A
  terminal/plain-editor footage and any re-shoots); the
  Playwright stills give the edit verified reference frames and
  poster/still assets for every site beat except 07.

Per PRODUCTION-PLAN §6 (operative) with the baseline §2/§4 mechanics:

- **Tool:** OBS Studio (free, open source) — per-beat short takes,
  separate audio tracks, no watermark, records at display
  resolution. AI/cloud recorders are rejected for hero footage (the
  demo's credibility is that it's real; compression tuned for faces
  destroys UI text).
- **Host:** **Will's recording machine** — not the Muse VM (OBS is
  deliberately not installed there) and not a ranch node. Browser
  zoom 125–150% so interface text survives YouTube compression;
  cookies cleared so the signed-out experience is on camera.
- **Cursor + text size (Will's direction, 2026-11-09 23:35 CST):**
  "grab a big video cursor and bump up the text size." Capture with
  a **large, high-visibility video cursor** (enlarged system cursor
  / cursor-highlight in OBS), and text size **bumped up — browser
  zoom at the top of the planned range (150%) and/or a larger
  editor font**. Recorded as Will's direction; the exact level is
  set on capture day against a test take.
- **Site version (confirmed 2026-11-09 23:35 CST):** production
  edit.phext.io is running **v1.1.0** (footer reads v1.1.0, per the
  main chat) — the settled build Session B was waiting for.
- **Resolution:** record at the display's native resolution —
  1440p or 4K canvas if the display allows; never upscale. Master
  composite is 1080p; graphics elements render at 2× and downscale.
- **Downstream (verified, see below):** all compositing/rendering on
  the ranch — aletheia-core as assembly point — stills → 720p
  prepass → 1080p master, under the thermal gates (pause new starts
  ≥75 °C Tctl, resume ≤70 °C). No video work on the Muse VM.
- **Narration is already rendered** (per-beat MP3s + full track,
  100% speed), so capture needs no mic decisions on the day; any
  captured audio track is scratch/reference only.

**Verified now (2026-11-09 23:32 CST):**
- Ranch: aletheia-core up 14 days, load average 0.88 / 1.29 / 0.82
  (light), **Tctl 43.9 °C** — ≈31 °C of headroom under the 75 °C
  pause gate; `ffmpeg` and `ffprobe` present at /usr/bin; 2.8 T
  free disk. (A point measurement, not a promise: this node's
  temperature has been driven high by other pipelines before —
  re-measure before any render session, per standing practice.)
- Demo environment: `demo/` runs on this VM under Python 3.12.3
  with zero setup (§2). The terminal block can be captured on any
  host with `python3` and the demo folder.

**Gaps that would block or bite on capture day:**
1. **The v1.1 gate — CLEARED (2026-11-09 23:35 CST):** production
   deploy of edit.phext.io v1.1.0 confirmed live (footer reads
   v1.1.0). Session B's remaining precondition is Will's upload of
   the feature phext (Beat 01) and the capture session itself.
   Session A was never affected. **Update (2026-11-10 00:00 CST):**
   the upload landed, but the /wiki/ surface is **sign-in walled
   anonymously** (verified by browser check + Playwright frame);
   Session B stills were captured via the anonymous Previewer +
   demo routes instead (see §4 amendment). A signed-in pass is
   still owed for: beat 01's wiki-in-editor frame, beat 07
   (edit + save), and — optionally — the editor's Search sheet,
   which automation could not hold open.
2. **OBS on the recording machine is unverified** — the plan's §1
   ledger records OBS as not installed on this VM (by design) and
   Will's local software state as unknown. Budget the install +
   two-scene build (browser, terminal) into capture-day setup;
   don't discover it mid-session.
3. **Capture display resolution unconfirmed** — the 1440p/4K plan
   depends on Will's display. If it's 1080p-only, capture at 1080p
   native and the 1080p master still works (graphics still render
   at 2×); just don't upscale the capture.
4. **`python3` on the capture machine unverified** — only matters
   if the terminal block is recorded there instead of on the
   VM/ranch. Five-second check on the day; the demo has no other
   dependency.
5. **Capture-day [CONFIRM] list** (WALKTHROUGH §5) resolves only
   against the settled site: signed-out demo phext + name, exact
   labels for navigation / coordinate jump / search / save, the
   beat-05 coordinate, and whether any visitor download exists for
   beat 08 (expected: no — fallback is the planned path).
6. **Assets not yet in hand** (don't block raw capture; block the
   edit): the §6.1 graphics package stills (Day-2 work) and the
   beat-12 Scrolltown key frame (§6.2, stage-5 commission +
   the 2026-12-04 register-lock dependency). Callouts composite in
