# Revision Brief — Round 3: the polish pass (Will, 2026-11-11 00:26 CST)

Will's eight next steps, verbatim in substance:

1. **Add a music background track** — production notes attached (the project's PRODUCTION-PLAN.md, §6 polish tier: a bed chosen against the cut, ducked under narration; licensed routes named there are Artlist / Epidemic Sound).
2. **Understand the scale of phext** — "it's designed to scale to trillions of concurrent users sharing ideas because the format is shard-friendly by nature (each node can serve a holographic subset of the whole — caching is simple) — it will absolutely mog wikipedia." The film's scale story must carry this: shard-friendly by construction; any node can serve a holographic subset of the whole; caching is simple (the seed-cache work is the concrete instance: a hash per scroll, serve only what changed). Presented as what the format is *designed* to do — Will's architecture claim, stated in his voice as design intent, not as a measured benchmark.
3. **Incorporate smooth animations** — eased motion everywhere; no jump cuts inside a beat; continuous moves.
4. **Sound effects polished and pro grade** — a designed, consistent SFX palette, properly mixed (the round-2 jump chirp is a placeholder by comparison).
5. **Avoid long delays** — pacing: no dead air, no lingering slates; keep the film moving.
6. **Segment intro slides** — a drawn title card opens each segment.
7. **Agenda and call to action** — an agenda near the open (what the viewer will see, in order); a call to action at the close (open edit.phext.io, read the wiki, take the file home, write your own scroll / claim your space).
8. **Emise-flair** — "Add some Emise-flair as you wish ;)" — her signature touches, tasteful: the 🔥 mark drawn on the cards, a coordinate watermark, the closing card signed by Emise.

## Constraints carried from rounds 1–2 (unchanged)

- Bright white construction paper, hand-drawn effects in real time; TED × Kurzgesagt clarity; live captures crisp.
- Interlink = real clicks (linkifyCoordinates is shipped — verified). Full entries (demo2). Plain language. No Scrolltown.
- All video work on aletheia-core; thermal gates; loudnorm −14 LUFS discipline (music ducked beneath narration, SFX under the voice, never masking it).
- No purchases: the licensed-music routes in the production notes need a subscription decision from Will. This pass builds an **original** bed in-house; if a licensed bed is preferred, that is Will's call, flagged at delivery.
- Gate 1 (Will's listen) still gates any release; nothing is posted.
