# Rough-Cut Log — REVISED cut ("The Encyclopedia You Can Carry")

**File:** `production/rough-cut-revised.mp4` — 1920×1080, 30 fps,
H.264 + AAC 192k, faststart. **Duration:** 253.03 s (video 253.03 s,
audio 253.00 s). **Size:** 49,333,014
bytes. **SHA-256** `495dbea2fe97cf54f0f31d72dc56e1f736993c432372c1dde583edbf44fd5c0a` (ranch build and pulled copy hash-identical)
**Built:** 2026-11-10, entirely on aletheia-core (ranch) — capture
reuse, drawn-asset rendering, segment encodes, and assembly all ran
there; this VM only coordinated, generated the narration via the TTS
route, and verifies the pulled file.
**Script:** `SCRIPT-EMI-REVISED.md` (Emi Prime's revision, delivered
by Will 2026-11-10 21:50 CST) — supersedes the 12-beat WALKTHROUGH.md
script. **Narration:** new render, Emise/Aria at 100% speed, 647
words, 223.37 s measured; per-section files + timing in
`narration-revised/`. Two-pass loudnorm to −14 LUFS; measured on the
finished file: **−14.41 LUFS integrated, −0.69 dBTP**.

## Style — TED × Kurzgesagt × Colored Pencil (Will, 2026-11-10 21:56 CST)

Applied as directed. The drawn layer is a set of stills and simple
frame sequences rendered with Pillow on the ranch
(`production/work-revised/drawn.py`, output in the ranch
`rev/drawn/`): warm paper texture, jittered multi-pass pencil
strokes, pencil-hatch fills, URW Bookman lettering with a chancery
script for accents. Live demo footage is **never textured over** —
it is framed on the paper texture inside a hand-drawn border, with
drawn lower-third strips. One idea per frame; the narration leads.

