## Capture facts

- Reused captures are the 2026-11-10 Playwright `recordVideo` takes
  of the live site (1920×1080, zoom 150%, big cursor), shot for the
  previous cut and re-framed here; no new browser capture was needed
  because the revised script's live-site beats match those takes.
- Terminal sections are new asciinema casts (104×34, agg, Monokai,
  font 20) recorded on aletheia-core against a scratch copy in
  `rev/demo-rev/`; the demo's pristine `wiki.phext` was never
  modified (SHA-256 `0a8dacf56843231b63ba717d590fac4d50fbef0076906d6fdeb96311c94262ae`).
- Drawn assets: Pillow 13 in a ranch venv; paper texture is seeded
  procedural noise + fibres + vignette; pencil strokes are
  multi-pass jittered lines. The cards-unfold motif is 75 frames at
  10 fps conformed to 30 fps (drawn-on-twos/threes feel).
- Assembly discipline matches the previous cut: segment encodes
  gated at ≤70 °C Tctl, 1080p30, CRF 18, loudnorm two-pass to
  −14 LUFS, faststart. Thermal gates held throughout: gate checks
  caught mid-run rises to 81.6 °C and held encodes until the node
  cooled; every segment encode started at ≤70 °C Tctl (starts
  recorded 36.6–70.5 °C, node ~64 °C at wrap). Two assembly faults
  were caught by verification and fixed before delivery: §02's first
  encode failed on a filter-graph stream reuse (one paper input
  feeding two overlays; fixed with explicit split filters), and
  §07's stills concat came up 2.93 s short of its slot (padded on
  its final, completed-song state). The delivered file's eight
  segment durations sum to the full 253.0 s slot table, and the
  pulled copy's SHA-256 matches the ranch build exactly.

## Gaps to the final cut

1. **§04** — Will's signed-in editor take still replaces the local
