# Rough-Cut Log — Round 2 ("The Encyclopedia You Can Carry")

**File:** `production/rough-cut-r2.mp4` — 1920×1080, 30 fps, H.264 +
AAC 192k, faststart. **Duration:** 292.2 s. **Size:** 102,109,905 bytes.
**SHA-256** `dd2b6e68ec30414ac1275be9b2444e718eed890940bd8f27daa28f23888b5e71` (ranch build and pulled copy hash-identical)
**Built:** 2026-11-10, entirely on aletheia-core (ranch) — capture,
drawn-asset rendering, segment encodes, and assembly all ran there;
this VM only coordinated, generated the narration via the TTS route,
and verifies the pulled file.
**Script:** `SCRIPT-R2.md` (Revision Round 2 per Will's notes of
2026-11-10 23:04 CST). **Narration:** Emise/Aria at 100% speed, 711
words, 234.05 s measured; per-section files + timing in
`narration-r2/`. Two-pass loudnorm to −14 LUFS; measured on the
finished file: **−14.45 LUFS integrated, −0.67 dBTP**.

## Correction applied mid-build (Will, via parent, 2026-11-10)

The original brief's "Phext Edit has no hyperlink layer" claim was
**wrong** and was corrected during production: in
wbic16/phext-lattice@exo, `linkifyCoordinates()` turns every
coordinate pattern in a rendered scroll into a clickable
`a.coord-link` that calls `gotoCoord(...)`. §06 was therefore filmed
as **actual clicks** — no prototype labels, no hedging. An earlier
draft of this log's framing (and §06's treatment plan) was revised
accordingly. Related: demo2 was rebuilt in parallel with coordinates
woven into article prose; all size figures below are the **final
rebuilt file's** measured numbers, not the pre-weaving ones.

## Demo facts (final rebuilt file, measured)

- `demo2/wiki.phext`: 119,086 bytes, 49 scrolls (24 articles +
  24 summaries + 1 home), SHA-256
  `7a7a4be95d530eb69c47fec91004b1724d5d4cdb3fc69432f659fe7ebf564130`
  (verified identical on this VM and on the ranch copy).
- xz −9 packed: 41,956 bytes (≈35% — "shrinks to a third").
- `verify_links.py` on the rebuilt file: 53 links, 24/24 articles
  reachable, travel path Honeybee → Oak → Sail → Compass →
  Lighthouse verified hop by hop, every linked coordinate also
  present inline in body prose — ALL LINK CHECKS PASSED.

## Click test (the claim source for the film's interlink statements)

Performed live on the local phext-edit instance serving demo2
(aletheia-core, `phext-edit wiki.phext --local --port 8902`,
binary `/home/wbic16/bin-new/phext-edit`):

- On the Honeybee scroll (1.1.1/2.1.1/2.1.1), the rebuilt file
  renders **6 `a.coord-link` elements** — 3 in the body prose + 3 in
  the Linked line (Oak 1.1.1/2.1.2/2.1.1, Coffee 1.1.1/2.5.4/2.1.1,
  Bread 1.1.1/2.5.1/2.1.1).
- Clicking the Oak coordinate landed the editor on exactly
  **1.1.1/2.1.2/2.1.1** with the Oak article text present —
  **PASS**, run twice (pre- and post-rebuild files; the post-rebuild
  run is the evidence of record). Evidence frames:
  `production/thumbs-r2/clicktest-before.png`,
  `clicktest-target.png`, `clicktest-after.png`.
- The §06 travel take repeats this for all four hops in one
  continuous recording; every landing was verified in the take's
  manifest (header coordinate read after each click): Oak click at
  6.07 s, Sail 18.27 s, Compass 30.19 s, Lighthouse 42.37 s — all
  `ok: true`.

## Style — bright white construction paper (Revision Brief R2)

The drawn layer is rendered with Pillow on the ranch
(`production/work-r2/drawn-r2.py`, output in the ranch `r2/drawn/`):
bright white paper (253,253,250, near-flat — *not* round 1's warm
sepia), hand-jittered multi-pass pencil strokes, and — per the
brief — strokes that **draw on in real time**: the 24-card unfold,
the map's 24 houses, the 53-thread link web, the pencil city, and
the end card are all progressive-stroke frame sequences, not fades
of finished drawings. The map and web use demo2's real data: titles
in TOC order, all 53 edges parsed from the articles' own Linked
lines. Live captures stay crisp, framed on the white paper inside a
hand-drawn border with drawn lower-thirds. One idea per frame.

## Per-section source map

Section boundaries are the narration-r2 TIMING.md slot starts.

| § | In cut | Source | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| 01 What if the website went away? | 0:00.0–0:26.0 | Drawn title card → drawn sequence: a browser window draws, is closed with a pencil X, the one file draws on, 24 cards (real titles) unfold → framed local-editor home capture | The "website closes" beat is drawn, not a live-site capture — see Gaps |
| 02 A place for every page | 0:26.0–0:56.0 | Framed Nav/TOC capture (local editor) → drawn coordinate card (the Oak's 1.1.1/2.1.2/2.1.1 in its three named groups) → framed Honeybee still → **ZOOM SET-PIECE #1** (drawn map: inside Honeybee → pull back to the whole map → dive to Oak) → framed Oak landing still (from the travel take) | SFX #1 on the dive's landing |
| 03 Finding your way back | 0:56.0–1:18.0 | Framed local-editor search capture: "mistletoe" typed (a phrase deep in the Oak article: "druids were said to gather mistletoe from it"), the result shows the Oak's address 1.1.1/2.1.2/2.1.1 with context, click → lands on the Oak | Capture trimmed so the filmed jump lands at the SFX mark; first search attempt failed on a hidden duplicate Search button — re-shot via the visible button (see log notes) |
