# demo2 — the FULL-entry mini encyclopedia in one phext file

Round 2 of the Phext Edit training-film demo (Revision Brief R2,
2026-11-10). Same 24 topics and the same coordinate scheme as `demo/`,
but every article is a **full encyclopedia entry** (600–900 words),
written original for this demo, and every article ends with a
**"Linked:" line** naming the other entries it points to — the
interlink layer, carried in the text itself.

The live site serves `demo/`'s file; demo2 is the film's working copy
and is never swapped into the site by this build.

## The file

- `wiki.phext` — the built encyclopedia: **119,086 bytes**, 49 scrolls
  (24 articles + 24 summaries + 1 home), SHA-256
  `7a7a4be95d530eb69c47fec91004b1724d5d4cdb3fc69432f659fe7ebf564130`.
- Packed with xz -9: **41,956 bytes** — about a third of its plain size.
- Rebuild: `python3 build_wiki2.py` (bodies live in `articles/<slug>.md`).
- Ask it things: `python3 query_demo2.py toc | get 1.1.1/2.1.2/2.1.1 | stats`
  — parse + index of the whole file measured at ~9 ms on the build
  machine; a single lookup is a dictionary hit (~1 µs).

## The link graph (verified, not asserted)

`python3 verify_links.py` parses the built file, reads every article's
Linked line, and checks: every target coordinate exists and holds the
named article; every linked entry is also named in the article's own
prose; the whole graph is one connected web; and the film's travel
path exists hop by hop. Result on this build: **ALL LINK CHECKS PASSED**.

- Total links: **53** (every article points to 2–3 others)
- Reachable from any single article: **24 / 24** — one web, no islands
- Article word counts: 703–800 words each (bodies, excluding Linked lines)
- The film's travel path, verified hop by hop:
  **Honeybee → Oak → Sail → Compass → Lighthouse**
  (1.1.1/2.1.1/2.1.1 → 1.1.1/2.1.2/2.1.1 → 1.1.1/2.3.2/2.1.1 →
  1.1.1/2.6.1/2.1.1 → 1.1.1/2.6.2/2.1.1)

## The one-scroll edit check (measured on a scratch copy)

Editing the Honeybee summary scroll (115 → 180 bytes) changed the file
119,086 → 119,151 bytes. Comparing before and after: the first 1,125
bytes and the last 117,962 bytes are identical — everything outside the
one edited scroll is byte-for-byte what it was; the only difference
lives inside that scroll.

## Coordinate scheme

Library.Shelf.Series / Collection.Volume.Book / Chapter.Section.Scroll
= 1.1.1 / 2.V.B / C.1.1 — Collection 2 is the encyclopedia,
Volume = topic area (1 The Living World, 2 Earth and Sky, 3 Human
Ingenuity, 4 Ideas and Numbers, 5 Everyday Science, 6 Exploration),
Book = article (1–4), Chapter 1 = summary, Chapter 2 = the article.
